!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-literal-argument-whose-type-is-still-open-in-an-operand-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.10"
  description: """
    `pin2` reads `P`'s argument as a value of `T`'s, and here `T` is bound to `X`, a parameter of `w` no
    application has fixed: the literal `3` has no type. A literal needs a closed type, so the application is
    refused where it is written. `pin2<int8, 3>` is a closed application and its member pins `a` to `3`.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
